<BaseLayout title="Troubleshooting" description="ABS delete, heat shielding, and common LS Gen Coupe swap issues.">
  <h1>Troubleshooting &amp; Common Jobs</h1>

  <h2>Heat Shielding</h2>
  <p>
    LS exhaust heat will cook the tunnel, floor, and nearby wiring if you don’t plan for it.
    Wrap headers, use tunnel heat shields, and protect fuel lines and brake lines.
  </p>

  <h2>ABS Delete</h2>
  <p>
    Some high-power builds remove the ABS hydraulic unit. If you do, the proportioning valve location matters for burnouts.
  </p>

